{{!
    @template tool_lp/competency_grader

    The rating dialogue's body, overridden by Dimensions.

    Mirrors tool_lp/competency_grader of Moodle 5.3 (2026100500), admin/tool/lp/templates/competency_grader.mustache.
    Re-diff it against that file on every core upgrade. tool_lp/grade_dialogue renders it into the
    "Rate" dialogue that every inline rating button opens (the user competency summaries, the
    breakdown report's popup).

    Kept from core, because tool_lp/grade_dialogue finds them inside the dialogue's content: the
    rate button's data-action="rate" (enabled only once a rating is chosen, and it fires the rating),
    the cancel button's data-action="cancel", the select named rating and the textarea named comment
    (read on rate), the regions data-region="competency-grader", "rating", "comment" and "footer",
    the ids rating_<uniqid> and comment_<uniqid> with their labels, and the form. Kept for Behat: the
    class competency-grader, which report_competency's feature scopes the rate button to. Every rating
    keeps its value and selected state; the names keep core's double stash.
    Changed: the fields are stacked with their labels above them (dim-comp-grader), the footer is a
    right-aligned row of the two buttons above a rule, and the clearfix is gone with the float.

    Data required for JS:
    * ratings - list of value, name and selected for the valid ratings

    Example context (json):
    {
        "ratings": [
            {"name": "Choose a rating", "value": ""},
            {"name": "Not yet competent", "value": 1},
            {"name": "Competent", "value": 2, "selected": true}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="competency-grader dim-comp-grader" data-region="competency-grader">
    <form>
        <div class="content">
            <div data-region="rating" class="dim-comp-grader__field">
                <label for="rating_{{uniqid}}">{{#str}}rating, tool_lp{{/str}}</label>
                <select name="rating" id="rating_{{uniqid}}" class="form-select">
                    {{#ratings}}
                        <option value="{{value}}" {{#selected}}selected{{/selected}}>{{name}}</option>
                    {{/ratings}}
                </select>
            </div>
            <div data-region="comment" class="dim-comp-grader__field">
                <label for="comment_{{uniqid}}">{{#str}}ratecomment, tool_lp{{/str}}</label>
                <textarea name="comment" id="comment_{{uniqid}}" class="form-control"></textarea>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div data-region="footer" class="dim-comp-grader__footer">
            <button data-action="rate" class="btn btn-primary">{{#str}}rate, tool_lp{{/str}}</button>
            <button data-action="cancel" class="btn btn-secondary">{{#str}}cancel{{/str}}</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</div>
